### UniBite — Test: POST /api/requests/pickup  +  /api/requests/no_show
### Run #1 first; the HTTP Client keeps the session cookie for the rest.
###
### PREP: pickup/no_show only work on APPROVED requests. So first create two
### pending requests and approve them (via the inbox or approve.php), OR insert
### them already-approved in phpMyAdmin (db unibite, SQL):
###   INSERT INTO requests (listing_id, consumer_id, slot, status, decided_at)
###   VALUES (2, 3, 1, 'approved', NOW()), (2, 3, 2, 'approved', NOW());
### Then read their ids from the `requests` table and put them below.

### 1) Login
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/auth/login.php
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "dimitris",
  "password": "unibite2025"
}

### 2) Mark request #1 as picked up (expect success; sets rate_deadline +48h)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/pickup.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=1

### 3) Mark request #2 as no-show (expect success + penalty_applied:true; consumer -1)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/no_show.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=2

### 4) Pickup #1 again (expect 409 Request is no longer approved)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/pickup.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=1
